%% Gaps:
%% - Trailmark's TypeScript graph treats UsherDoor as a module node without edges. The authorize path is in UsherDoor and door-v3.ts; confirm against those sources.
%% - A passkey session alone is not a ticket. Unpaid tickets, second uses, and removed ushers are refused.
flowchart TB

    GuestTicket["pages/ticket.tsx · Your ticket QR"]:::guest --> ShowQr["Guest shows Door ticket QR"]:::guest
    UsherPage["pages/check-in.tsx · Check-in"]:::usher --> Gate["isSignedInUsher / CheckInPanel"]:::usher
    Gate --> Door["UsherDoor stages: scan, proving, authorize, done"]:::usher
    Door --> Cam["Select Open camera"]:::usher
    Door --> Photo["Select Scan a ticket photo"]:::usher
    Cam --> Scan["scanFile / startCamera reads the QR"]:::usher
    Photo --> Scan
    ShowQr --> Scan
    Scan --> ProveUi["Building the door proof…"]:::usher
    ProveUi --> Prepare["prepareConsumeV3"]:::usher
    Prepare --> CircuitProve["circuits/sezs-ticket-v2 prove"]:::chain
    CircuitProve --> Authorize["Select Authorize with Zafu"]:::wallet
    Authorize --> Submit["submitConsumeV3"]:::usher
    Submit --> Execute["cw-event-manifold execute ConsumeTicket"]:::chain
    Execute --> Verify["verify_ticket_proof"]:::chain
    Verify --> Admitted["Door note: admitted"]:::chain
    Verify --> Refused["Door note: refused"]:::chain
    Admitted --> Next["Select Next guest"]:::usher
    Refused --> Next

